# Storybook Story Conventions

Every component in `src/components/ui/` **must** have a co-located
`<component>.stories.tsx` file before the component is considered done.

## Minimum required exports

| Export | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `default` (meta) | `title`, `component`, `tags: ['autodocs']`, `argTypes` |
| `AllVariants` | Full visual showcase — all variants, sizes, states |
| At least one named story per distinct feature | e.g. `WithIcon`, `Disabled`, `Loading` |

## File template

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/nextjs-vite'
import { MyComponent } from './my-component'

const meta = {
  title: 'UI/MyComponent',
  component: MyComponent,
  tags: ['autodocs'],
  parameters: { layout: 'centered' },
  argTypes: {
    variant: {
      control: 'select',
      options: ['default', 'outline', 'destructive'],
    },
  },
} satisfies Meta<typeof MyComponent>

export default meta
type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>

export const AllVariants: Story = {
  name: 'Showcase — All Variants',
  render: args => (
    <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2 p-4">
      <MyComponent variant="default" {...args}>Default</MyComponent>
      <MyComponent variant="outline" {...args}>Outline</MyComponent>
      <MyComponent variant="destructive" {...args}>Destructive</MyComponent>
    </div>
  ),
}

export const Default: Story = {
  args: { children: 'Label' },
}
```

## Rules

- `title` must follow the pattern `'UI/<ComponentName>'`.
- Always add `tags: ['autodocs']` so props documentation is auto-generated.
- Use `render:` for showcase stories; use `args:` for individual stories.
- Icon-only interactive elements in stories must have `aria-label`.
- Do **not** import from `@storybook/react` — always use `@storybook/nextjs-vite`.
- Stories that need server-side data must mock it locally inside the story file.
